<urn:atm:triage:finding/RSH-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RSH-002" ;
  triage:title "The request-size limit is enforced today on the final wire body, after the splice. `prepare` compares body.len() to the descriptor's request_limit_bytes and returns InputTooLarge (check.rs:62-66). r-5 deletes splice_model and `prepare`'s path, and deliverables 1 and 3 say no other schema check remains. They never say where the limit is checked against the new CheckRequest::to_body output. The documented Jev body is larger than the canonical bytes (criteria maps, descriptions, model, instructions). A check on the canonical payload would pass bodies that exceed the Jev limit. Dropping the check would send an unbounded body and rely on the server to reject it. Recommendation: State in deliverable 3 that sc-jev compares the length of to_body() output to the Jev descriptor's request_limit_bytes before send. It should return InputTooLarge with the same limit and actual-byte fields as today. This is the existing check moved onto the new builder, not a new gate. Haiku and Luna keep enforce_count_and_message_limits unchanged." ;
  triage:description "The request-size limit is enforced today on the final wire body, after the splice. `prepare` compares body.len() to the descriptor's request_limit_bytes and returns InputTooLarge (check.rs:62-66). r-5 deletes splice_model and `prepare`'s path, and deliverables 1 and 3 say no other schema check remains. They never say where the limit is checked against the new CheckRequest::to_body output. The documented Jev body is larger than the canonical bytes (criteria maps, descriptions, model, instructions). A check on the canonical payload would pass bodies that exceed the Jev limit. Dropping the check would send an unbounded body and rely on the server to reject it. Recommendation: State in deliverable 3 that sc-jev compares the length of to_body() output to the Jev descriptor's request_limit_bytes before send. It should return InputTooLarge with the same limit and actual-byte fields as today. This is the existing check moved onto the new builder, not a new gate. Haiku and Luna keep enforce_count_and_message_limits unchanged." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
